-- title:
--   Finiteness of H¹(D) and duality with Ω_F(D)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a perfect field and $F$ a field extension of $K$ that is essentially of finite type and satisfies `IsCurveOver K F`: every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a finitely supported divisor $D$ with $D(v) = v.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at every place $v$ and $\deg D = 0$, each residue field of a place is finite-dimensional over $K$, and the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one over $F$; here a place is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring. Assume in addition `ConstantsAreBase K F`, i.e. the Riemann–Roch space of the zero divisor equals the image of $K$ in $F$. Let $D$ be a divisor, i.e. a finitely supported function from places to $\mathbb{Z}$. Write $H^1(D)$ for the quotient of the répartition algebra `repartitions K F` (the $F$-subalgebra of $\prod_v F$ generated by the families $\alpha$ with $v(\alpha_v) > 1$ for only finitely many $v$) by the sum of the submodule of répartitions satisfying $v(\alpha_v) \le \exp(D(v))$ for all $v$ and the diagonal image of $F$. The assertion is twofold: $H^1(D)$ is finite-dimensional over $K$, and there is a $K$-linear isomorphism $e$ from the $K$-dual of $H^1(D)$ onto `omegaSpace D`, the annihilator in the dual of the adèle space $\mathbb{A} = \bigsqcup_E \mathbb{A}(E)$ of the submodule `adeleBddPrincipal K F D` (the preimage in $\mathbb{A}$ of the $D$-bounded adèles together with the preimage of `globalSub K F`), characterised by the property that for every functional $\varphi$ on $H^1(D)$ and every adèle $a$ whose underlying family is a répartition, $e(\varphi)$ evaluated at $a$ equals $\varphi$ applied to the class of that répartition in $H^1(D)$.
--
--   This is Serre duality for a curve in Weil's adelic formulation at the level of function fields over a perfect base: the dual of the répartition cohomology $H^1(D) = \mathbb{A}/(\mathbb{A}(D)+F)$ is the space of Weil differentials bounded by $D$. It supports the bijectivity of the Serre pairing ([`AlgebraicCurve.serrePairing_bijective_and_flip_bijective`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.serrePairing_bijective_and_flip_bijective)) and the finite-dimensionality of spaces of differentials on modular curves ([`ModularCurve.finiteDimensional_omegaSpace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finiteDimensional_omegaSpace)).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_finite_H1_and_exists_linearEquiv_dual_H1_omegaSpace.lean

